        "original_id": "570bb955-835e-565b-bb3f-fd201a6e7246",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Lovell, Jeffrey Kluger\n- Products: Lost Moon, Apollo 13\n- Organizations: NASA, United States Navy\n- Events: Apollo 13 mission\n\nFacts:\n- James Arthur Lovell Jr. was born on March 25, 1928.\n- In April 1970, the Apollo 13 lunar landing mission suffered a critical failure on the way to the Moon, and the crew and mission control brought it back safely to Earth.\n- James Lovell commanded the failed Apollo 13 lunar landing mission.\n- James Lovell is a former NASA astronaut and a retired captain in the United States Navy.\n- In 1994, astronaut James Lovell and journalist Jeffrey Kluger first published the non-fiction book Lost Moon: The Perilous Voyage of Apollo 13.\n- Lost Moon was later published in paperback as Apollo 13.\n- Lost Moon is about the failed April 1970 Apollo 13 lunar landing mission.",
